cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Indian Railway Network Station-Level Physical Graph (Rail-Intell graph v1.4)
message: >-
  If you use this dataset, please cite it. Read
  graph_v1_4/FITNESS.md first: it states which conclusions this graph supports
  and which it does not, and 25.3% of its route km is a lower bound rather than
  a measurement. docs/STABILITY.md is the engineering contract.
type: dataset
version: "1.4"
date-released: "2026-10-12"
abstract: >-
  A reproducible, validated station-level physical graph of the Indian railway
  network: 9,095 nodes (stations and operational junctions) and 9,759 physical
  track sections spanning 74,849.7 route km, with 99.59% of nodes in a single
  connected component. Constructed from national railway GIS polylines by
  corridor spine reconstruction, station projection and junction stitching, then
  repaired against three independent references that were never used in
  construction. Released as a gated, deterministic build with a content-hashed
  manifest, a recorded decision trail of 179 evidence-carrying overrides, a
  construction-choice sensitivity study, a stability contract with a regression
  test suite, and a documented register of its own defects. Nine release gates
  must pass for a build to ship; route lengths agree with the 2024 timetable to a
  median 0.72%, with 95.69% of train routes within 5%.
keywords:
  - railway network
  - Indian Railways
  - spatial network
  - network science
  - infrastructure
  - graph dataset
  - reproducibility
  - FAIR data
authors:
  - family-names: Vinjamuri
    given-names: Bhuvanesh
    email: vinjamuri.bhuvan@gmail.com
    roles:
      - Data engineering and provenance
license-note: >-
  Code is MIT and prose is CC BY 4.0 (see LICENSES.md). The dataset itself is not
  yet licensable: it derives from a GIS source whose redistribution terms are
  restrictive (publication/SOURCE_LICENCE_INVENTORY.md section 8), so the graph is
  described and fully reproducible from the pipeline, with deposit pending a
  rebuild from open inputs.
